Expected elements: present

All four changes landed. The provenance note now sets flush-left in its own full-width row under `DATA` (y 205-380); the fee reads `1755555891986239551 mana (FeeJuice)` in base ten; the decoded-input note is a distinct sentence for this state; and no `aztec` slug or demo-fixture content appears — the exit reads `← aztec-testnet`, the facts are testnet. No band above the identity bar. The queued enum, `Status reason: private-part-succeeded-public-part-succeeded`, is gone from the visible viewport; status is carried by the `Succeeded` pill alone.

But the same defect class survives twice. `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` (1543,555) is still a camelCase key uppercased, alone among English labels. And the replay telemetry — `effectsMismatched: 0`, this view's faithfulness evidence — exists only as camelCase JSON inside `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)`, and the provenance paragraph's ~175px pushed it below the 1080 fold. The band's cost was relocated into the busiest pane, not removed.

The three source-starved paragraphs are excellent and in one voice; each blames the chain, not the product. Two nits: the Code pane's second paragraph restates its first, and "This tree holds no call data" leaks an internal noun.

Register: three green pills mean three unrelated things; and in light theme pane interiors and canvas are both white on a hairline, so a legitimately empty session reads as a failed render.

Fixes: promote effects matched/mismatched to a labelled row above the raw block; rename the fee label.

Rating: 6/10

